# The committed dist/ bundles must be byte-identical when CI rebuilds them
# from source (see .buildkite/commands/run-lint.sh). Newlines inside template
# literals end up in the bundle bytes, so a CRLF checkout would build bundles
# that differ from CI's LF build. Pin LF for everything in this package.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated bundles conflict on every concurrent PR that regenerates them,
# even when the underlying source changes don't overlap, because they're
# minified and any two rebuilds differ byte-for-byte. Hand-merging them is
# also unsafe: a textual merge can produce a file that merges cleanly and is
# wrong. Take one side instead of merging, then regenerate with
# `npm run build:mcp-bundle` and let CI's "Verify committed plugin bundles"
# step confirm the committed bytes match a fresh build. Never resolve a
# conflict on these files by hand-merging the hunks.
dist/mcp-server.bundle.mjs merge=ours
dist/capture-engine.bundle.mjs merge=ours
